[   94.673014]: buttons: next: read the type of the PMK8550's power-on block through channel 533 (2 registers, 0x1304)
[   94.673027]: buttons: the PMK8550's power-on block says type 0x1, subtype 0x9 (the read took 6 us)
[   94.673030]: buttons: next: read the type of GPIO6 of the PM8550 through channel 559 (2 registers, 0x8d04)
[   94.673042]: buttons: GPIO6 of the PM8550 says type 0x10, subtype 0x13 (the read took 6 us)
[   94.673045]: buttons: step 4: how the keys' inputs are set up
[   94.673048]: buttons: next: read the status and the interrupt setup of the PMK8550's power-on block (registers 0x1310 to 0x1319)
[   94.673078]: buttons: power-on block: status 0x18 (power released, volume up released); interrupts: edge 0, high 0, low 0, enabled 0, latched 0, pending 0
[   94.673081]: buttons: next: read the setup and the level of GPIO6 of the PM8550 (registers 0x8d40 to 0x8d47, 0x8d10)
[   94.673111]: buttons: volume down's pin: mode 0 (input), supply 1, pull 0 (up), enabled; registers 0x40.. = 00 01 00 00 00 01 80 00; level high (released)
[   94.673114]: buttons: step 5: watching power volume-up volume-down, every 16 ms: power is the side button
